      "problem": "Given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{4x+2}{(x+2)(x-1)}=\\frac{A}{(x+2)}+\\frac{2}{(x-1)},\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $A?$",
      "worked_solution": "Our task is to find $A$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4x+2}{(x+2)(x-1)}=\\frac{A}{(x+2)}+\\frac{2}{(x-1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(x+2)(x-1)$ gives\n\n$$\n4x+2=A(x-1)+2(x+2).\n$$\n\nFor $x=-2$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(-2)+2 & =A(-2-1)+2(-2+2) \\\\ -6 & =-3A \\\\ A & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
